      "anchor": {
        "mission_intent": "We need a full specification for the Secure Operations Management Module within our enterprise platform, aligned with NIST SP 800-160 Volume 1 guidance on managing results of secure operation. The module must provide automated recording of all secure operation results and any security anomalies encountered during system runtime, with specific emphasis on capturing data related to the correctness, effectiveness, and practicality of the operation strategy, the operation of enabling systems, the execution of operations, and system definition elements. It must also implement a structured incident and problem tracking capability that records security aspects of operational incidents, links them to observed system behavior and associated outcomes, and tracks each issue through to resolution. The design should integrate with our existing Project Assessment and Control process so that recorded data feeds into root-cause analysis workflows, supports corrective and improvement actions, and captures lessons learned in a retrievable format. The specification must reference applicable controls from ISO/IEC 12207 Section 6.4.9, ISO/IEC 21827, NIST SP 800-37, NIST SP 800-53A, and NIST SP 800-137 as normative sources, and should define role-based access, audit trail integrity, and retention policies for all recorded operational and incident data. Please have a draft ready for architecture review by end of next sprint.",
